        "original_id": "7846c7dc-4c58-575d-88a1-3379ffc0b7b1",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Works: We Are Your Friends\n- People: Max Joseph, Meaghan Oppenheimer, Richard Silverman, Zac Efron, Emily Ratajkowski, Wes Bentley, Robin Thicke\n- Places: London, California, Los Angeles\n- Topics: directorial debut, music videos, music industry controversy\n\nFacts:\n- Emily Ratajkowski was born to American parents in London and was raised primarily in California.\n- In 2013, Emily Ratajkowski rose to prominence after appearing in Robin Thicke's music video for \"Blurred Lines.\"\n- In 2013, Robin Thicke's \"Blurred Lines\" became the number one song of the year in several countries and attracted controversy over its purportedly sexist content.\n- In 2015, \"We Are Your Friends\" was released as a drama film directed by Max Joseph in his directorial debut.\n- \"We Are Your Friends\" was written by Max Joseph and Meaghan Oppenheimer from a story by Richard Silverman.\n- \"We Are Your Friends\" stars Zac Efron, Emily Ratajkowski, and Wes Bentley.\n- \"We Are Your Friends\" follows a young Los Angeles DJ trying to succeed in the music industry and figure out life with his friends.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
